Enhancement: Remove the data of excluded files with `rewrite --forget --prune`

`restic rewrite --exclude ... --forget` removed files from snapshots, but their
data stayed in the repository until a `prune` run repacked the pack files that
held it. Depending on its `--max-unused` limit, `prune` could keep that data
indefinitely, for example a small file stored next to data that is still used.

The new `--prune` option of `rewrite` requires `--forget`. After rewriting the
snapshots, restic runs `prune` with its default options and additionally
repacks every pack file that holds data only the original snapshots referenced.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22193
